{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And the word וירד [\"and He came down\"].</b> Because all the deeds of the lower beings depend on the power of the higher ones, and from the heavens all actions are governed — therefore the Name is called \"rider of the heavens\" (Deuteronomy 33:26), \"who sits in the heavens\" (Psalms 123:1) — and in the manner of human speech Scripture said וירד [\"and He came down\"]."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The phrase לשון בני אדם (\"language of human beings\") signals Ibn Ezra's standard position that biblical anthropomorphic expressions use human idiom."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:08.764178082Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}